# Collaboration & Portal Role

**Tool adapter**: Project truth and agent capabilities live in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md](../../AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md). This file extends those canonical sources with tool-specific context; it must not override them. Keep in sync with AGENTS.md.

## Reference: internal catalog reference product
This project aligns with an **internal catalog reference product** (private mirror; registered in platform-command registry, not named here). When extending conventions or tooling, prefer consistency with that reference:
- **docs/**: architecture, conventions, runbooks, product (engineering knowledge layer). **specs/**: API and schema contracts.
- **.vscode**: format on save, Prettier as default formatter, ESLint on save; extensions for ESLint, Prettier, Vitest, GitLens, Tailwind, Path IntelliSense, Auto Close/Rename Tag, etc.
- **Architecture**: features in `app/features/*`; shared/cross-module in shared layer; routes thin. (The reference also has legacy `app/module/` and uses `app/store/`, `app/lib/`, `app/mocks/`; ai-search-portal uses `app/shared/*`, `app/services/*` and MSW in `app/test/`.)

## Portal Role
This app is the **skeleton/portal** that aggregates and organizes multiple information systems. New features and routes are modular entry points; shared logic in `app/shared/*`, app-level integration in `app/services/*`. Keep routes thin—coordinate UI and data only.

## Two Strategic Directions
- **Clean Architecture (business spec as hub)**：docs/product is the project hub; all features trace to specs; dependency inward. See `docs/architecture/clean-architecture.md`.
- **Semi-automated UI / Design System**：Single source for tokens and components; see `docs/architecture/design-system.md` and `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`.

## Directory & Data Flow
- **Five-layer repo**（product vs platform）：**app** (shell) | **features** | **components** | **services** | **infra** (optional). Full mapping: `docs/architecture/repo-layers.md`.
- **Features** (`app/features/*`): `*.hooks.ts`, `*.server.ts`, `*.types.ts`. UI calls hooks; hooks use loaders/actions; server logic in `*.server.ts`. No feature→feature dependency.
- **Shared** (`app/shared/*`): contracts, api, services, types, utils. Cross-module coordination via `app/shared/services`.
- **App services** (`app/services/*`): integration and computation. Routes in `app/routes/*` do not contain business logic.

## Quality & CI
- Before PR: `pnpm run lint`, `pnpm run typecheck`, `pnpm run test`, `pnpm run lint:filenames`.
- CI: lint:filenames, ESLint strict, typecheck, test; Knip optional until tuned.
- User-facing changes: `pnpm run changeset`. Commits: Conventional Commits (commitlint).

## Workspace Alignment
- **.vscode**: `settings.json` enforces format on save, ESLint, Prettier, Tailwind, non-relative TS imports. `extensions.json` recommends the stack in `docs/VSCODE.md` (ESLint, Prettier, Tailwind, Vitest, GitLens, TypeScript Hero, Path Intellisense, Project Manager, etc.) for large-scale collaboration.
- **Docs**: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`, `docs/CONVENTIONS.md`, `docs/README.md` are the source of truth for structure and workflow.
- **Domain / product**: `docs/product/` (overview, domain models, LUI, Items API, release notes, mock strategy). Mock/seed: `docs/product/mock-data.md`, `docs/conventions/mock-dataset-versioning.md`.
- **Data-test-driven**：Spec → Contract → Mock → Test → UI. Schema: Zod in `app/shared/contracts/`; every API has MSW handler; no direct fetch in components; CI: `lint:handlers`. See `docs/conventions/data-test-driven.md`, `specs/api/contract-schema.md`, `specs/api/handler-mapping.md`, `app/shared/api/README.md`.
